        "root_concepts": "[sql, core]",
        "section": "query-languages",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "SQL Core - The 30-Year Refresh",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSQL Server 2000 era (your baseline)          What was added since\n─────────────────────────────────────────    ──────────────────────────────────────────\nSELECT / FROM / WHERE / JOIN                 [same] still the same\nGROUP BY / HAVING                            [same] still the same\nSubqueries (correlated + uncorrelated)       [same] still the same\nBasic transactions (BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK)   [same] still the same\nStored procedures / triggers                 [same] still the same (more features added)\nTOP n (T-SQL)                                → FETCH FIRST n ROWS ONLY (ANSI SQL:2008)\n                                             → LIMIT n (PostgreSQL/MySQL shorthand)"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-SQL-CORE.md#009",
      "path": [
        "01-SQL-CORE.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:query-languages:01-sql-core, git-history:query-languages:01-sql-core]",
